1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1894-1895 Cavalry Officer Candidate School (Kavalleriets officersaspirantskola, KavOAS), The Royal Swedish Army
2 CONT 1895-1900 Second Lieutenant (Underlöjtnant) at Scania Cavalry Regiment (Skånska Husarregementet), The Royal Swedish Army
2 CONT 1900-1908 Lieutenant (Löjtnant) at Scania Cavalry Regiment (Skånska Husarregementet), The Royal Swedish Army
2 CONT 1908-1910 Lieutenant (Löjtnant) of the Reserve at Scania Cavalry Regiment (Skånska Husarregementet), The Royal Swedish Army
2 CONT 1910-1963 Cavalry Captain (Ryttmästare) of the Reserve (to disposition from 1921) at Scania Cavalry Regiment (Skånska Husarregementet), The Royal Swedish Army
2 CONT 1908-1918 President & CEO, of  Baltiska Trävaru, AB, and Töre, AB
2 CONT 1918-1921 President & CEO Wifstavarfs, AB, Timrå, Sweden
2 CONT 1921-1926 Envoyé (Minister) of Sweden  in Washington.
2 CONT 1928-xxxx The International Committee on Newsprint (Ticon)
2 CONT Member of the Board of Directors of Kopparberg & Hofors Sågverks, AB – later Kopparfors AB, Storviks Sulfit, AB, Wifstavarfs, AB, Stockholms Strumpfabrik, AB Stockholms Enskilda Bank, AB (now Skadinaviska Enskilda Banken, AB) (194
2 CONC 0-1958), Stockholm, Sweden, Hambros Bank Ltd. (London, England, the United Kingdom, and the Knut and Alice Wallenberg’s Foundation (Knut och Alice Wallenbergs Stiftelse) (1939-1946)
2 CONT Chairman of the Board of Directors of Wifstavarfs, AB, Kopparfors AB (until 1960), Arbrå Kraftverk AB, and Rederiet Väring (Founder), and and Knut and Alice Wallenbergs Foundation (Knut och Alice Wallenbergs Stiftelse) (1946-1961)
2 CONT 1906-1921 Chairman of the Executive Committee for Swedish Lawn Tennis Association
2 CONT 1916-1921 Member of the Executive Committee for The Royal Automobile Club
2 CONT 1926-1928 Chairman of the Executive Committee for Swedish Lawn Tennis Association 
2 CONT 1932-1937 Member of the Executive Committee for The Royal Automobile Club
2 CONT 1935-1941 Chairman of the Executive Committee for Stockholms Kapplopningsselskab
2 CONT 1944-19xx Chairman of the Executive Committee for Stockholms Golf Club (Stockholms Golfklubb)
2 CONT 1901 Co-Founder of Foreningen til Fagtkonstens Fremmende 
2 CONT Stockholms Skridskoseglarklubb (tennis)
2 CONT 1951 Honorary Member of the Lantbruksakademiet – later Skogs- & Lantbruksakademiet
2 CONT 1954 Honorary Medical Doctor, Stockolms Karolininska Institute, Stockholm, Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT N.B.
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut and Alice Wallenberg’s Foundation was the largest shareholder in Förvaltnings AB Providentia – merged into AB Investor, and in AB Investor, which was / is the largest Swedish holding companies and they was / is the controllin
