1 NAME Emilie /Smith/
2 GIVN Emilie
2 SURN Smith
2 _MARNM Flygare-Carlén
1 NAME Emilie Flygare Carlén
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 8 AUG 1807
2 ADDR
3 CITY Strömstad
3 STAE Västra Götaland County
3 CTRY Sweden
1 DEAT
2 DATE 5 FEB 1892
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 10 Kommendörsgatan
3 CITY Stockholm
3 STAE Stockholms län
3 POST 114 48
3 CTRY Sweden
1 BURI
2 DATE 14 FEB 1892
2 PLAC Norra begravningsplatsen i Solna
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Författare, Author, Novelist, Celebrated Swedish novelist
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Author.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emelie was the youngest of 14 siblings, the daughter of Margareta Stiegler and the merchant and naval Captain Rutger Smith who at Mödernet was of a Scottish family. Her childhood home was quite nice and they had it well off. At th
2 CONC e age of 12 she had to accompany her father on freight travel on the Bohus coast. When she was 17, she had to take responsibility for a boat; She has experienced the environs that she writes about in her Bohus books.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married in 1827 to Doctor Axel aviator, and they had 4 children together. Two of these died as babies. The family lived in Sunnerbo, where her husband worked as a provinsialläkare. In 1833 her husband died and Emelie was widow
2 CONC ed. She and the children moved back to their home district. After a small time, she was engaged to a lawyer Jakob Reinhold Dalin. She became pregnant, but before the couple could marry Dalin got gangrene in a leg and died shortly 
2 CONC before the wedding. In 1836 she gave birth to his daughter, Rosaura, who was adopted the following year by Reinhold Dalin's relatives. The same year, Emelie died.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''references:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT *Emelie Flygare-Carléns texter på svenska finns tillgängliga på [http://runeberg.org/authors/flygare.html Projekt Runeberg] *[http://runeberg.org/authors/flygare.html Bibliografi] över tillgängliga böcker av Emelie Flygare-Carlén 
2 CONC på Projekt Runeberg.
2 CONT
