1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Carl Bonde=
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Wikipedia===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Bonde '''''Carl'' Gustaf Bonde af Björnö'''] was a Swedish Count, Army officer, equerry and horse rider who competed at the 1912 and 1928 Olympics.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Military career===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bonde was born in''' Stockholm, Sweden and was the son of landowner, count '''Gustaf ''Fredrik'' Bonde af Björnö''' and his English wife '''''Ida'' Horatia Charlotta Marryat'''. After passing his studentexamen in 1892, Bonde be
2 CONC came a sergeant in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_Regiment_Hussars '''Life Regiment Hussars'''] (K 3) in 1893 and second lieutenant in 1894 and lieutenant there in 1900. He retired in 1908 and became cavalry captain in th
2 CONC e reserve in 1910. The year before, in 1909, Bonde was appointed Equerry of the court, and advanced in 1916 to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crown_Equerry_(Sweden%29 Crown Equerry], a position he held for decades.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sports career===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bonde was a prominent''' horse rider. In 1912 he won the gold medal in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equestrian_at_the_1912_Summer_Olympics_%E2%80%93_Individual_dressage individual dressage competition] with his horse Empe
2 CONC ror. Sixteen years later he won the silver medal as a member of the Swedish team. He also competed in the 1928 Olympic individual dressage competition with his horse Ingo and finished 19th.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Other work===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bonde possessed a''' wide range of entailed estates, including [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vibyholm_Castle Vibyholm Castle] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/H%C3%B6rningsholm_Castle Hörningsholm Castle] in Södermanland, Ka
2 CONC trineholm, Bordsjö, Askeryd and [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herrestad,_Marb%C3%A4ck Herrestad] in Småland and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%A4vstaholm Sävstaholm] and [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toftaholm Toftaholm]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was a member''' of Halland County Rural Economy and Agricultural Societie's acquisition committee (Hallands läns hushållningssällskaps förvärvsutskott) and member of the Halland County landstorm. Bonde was an inspector of PO
2 CONC W camps in Siberia from 1917 to 1918.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' He was chairman''' of the Stockholm Harness Horseman's Association from 1900 and chairman and vice chairman of the Swedish Equestrian Central Association in 1933-1938. He served as a judge of equestrian competitions at the 193
2 CONC 2 Olympics in Los Angeles.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Personal life===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bonde was married''' and divorced twice. He was married 1896–1919 to '''''Blanche'' Charlotte Eleonore Dickson''' (1875-1960), daughter of James Fredrik Dickson and Blanche Dickson. Bonde was married a second time 1920-1941 to 
2 CONC [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Wallenberg#TAB_6 '''Ebba Wallenberg'''] (1896-1960), daughter of the banker [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcus_Wallenberg_Sr '''Marcus Wallenberg, Sr''']. and Amalia Hagdahl. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In the first marriage''' he was the father of Chief of the Army, Lieutenant General Thord Bonde and Colonel Carl C:son Bonde, and in the latter Peder Bonde, chamberlain and active in the so-called ''Wallenberg sphere''.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bonde's first wife''' Blanche Dickson inherited [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tjol%C3%B6holm_Castle Tjolöholm Castle] and they lived there until their divorce in 1919. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Adelsvapen==
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Bonde_af_Bj%C3%B6rn%C3%B6_nr_41#TAB_8 '''''Carl'' Gustaf Bonde af Björnö'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Huvudman och''' fideikommissarie efter fadern 1909. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Född 1872-04-28''' på Hörningsholm i Mörkö förs., Södermanlands län. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Volontär vid Livregementets''' husarer 1891. Mogenhetsexamen 1892. Sergeant 1893. Elev vid Krigsskolan 1893. Utexaminerad 1894. Underlöjtnant i regementet 1894 och vid regementet 1897. Löjtnant i regementet 1900 och vid regemen
2 CONC tet 1903. BMi1K1kl 1905. RRS:tA03kl 1907. Avsked med tillstånd att inträda i regementets reserv 1908. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Stallmästare i Kunglig''' Majestäts hov 1909. RRS:tAO2kl 1909. OffFrd'A 1909. Ryttmästare i regementets reserv 1910. GV:sOIM 1912. Hovstallmästare 1916. RVO 1917. RSO 1919. PrRK M 1, 2 o. 3 kl. ÖRKHt2kl med krigsdek. KVO2kl 192
2 CONC 8. KBeopO. GV:sJmt. StOffLettSO. GMsjv. TurkRHalvM. 2GM. KVO1kl 1948. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inneh. fideikommissegendomarna''' i Vibyholm och Hörningsholm i Södermanland, ävensom Katrineholm, Bordsjö, Askeryd och Herrestad i Småland samt Sävstaholms och Toftaholms fideikommisskapital. (EÄ Tillträdde efter faderns död 1
2 CONC 909 de av honom innehavda fideikommissegendomarna, av vilka Säfstaholm och Toftaholm sedermera förbytts till fideikommisskapital.) Ägde Tjolöholm i Fjärås socken, Hallands län och äger hus i Stockholm. Biogr i ''Vem är det''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Död 1957-06-13''' på [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/H%C3%B6rningsholms_slott Hörningsholm] i Mörkö förs., Södermanlands län (db).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1:o 1896-05-12''' i Hagakyrkan i Göteborg med '''''Blanche'' Charlotte Eleonore Dickson''', från vilken han blev skild 1920, född 1875-07-15 iGöteborgs (Domkyrkoförs.), död 1960-08-20 i Fjärås förs., Hallands län (db), dot
2 CONC ter av stallmästaren James Fredrik Dickson och Cecilia Blanche Charlotte Dickson.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 2:o 1920-06-21''' i Svenska kyrkan i Köpenhamn (Skeppsholms förs. i Stockholm, vb) med [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Wallenberg#TAB_6 '''Ebba Wallenberg'''] från vilken han blev skild genom Stockholms rådhusrätt do
2 CONC m. 1941-05-27, född 1896-11-21 i Stockholm. FinlVRO:sHt 1940-11-25. Död 1960-05-21 i Stockholm (Hedvig Eleonora förs., db). Dotter av bankdirektören, vice häradshövdingen Marcus Laurentius Wallenberg och Gertrud Amalia Hagdahl.
