1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcus_Wallenberg_Jr._
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcus Wallenberg was a Swedish banker and business manager. He was the most influential representative for the Swedish industrial tradition and Swedish business’ during the 20th century. He was the CEO of Stockholms Enskilda Bank
2 CONC  1946–1958 and during half a century – from the early 1930s until his death 1982 – he led and reconstructed many of Sweden's largest companies. During WWII Marcus together with Erik Boheman were appointed to conduct the Swedish tr
2 CONC ade negotiations.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcus had a big interest in sailing and tennis. He participated in the 1936 Olympic games and was a Swedish elite tennis player. He received a technological honorary degree from Royal Institute of Technology.
2 CONT ----
